  "conclusion": "corresponds",
  "rationale": "Comparison for unit:shared.typing.preservation against lean:Shared/TypingSafety:ConfigurationTyped.preservation. The public preservation theorem quantifies over any extended Step from a typed configuration and retains finalEnvironment. Its existential current environment may change. The definition of static give explains why a shared copy preserves descriptions despite promoting a stored final reference, while subsequent binding extends the environment. Notation and judgment context was checked in unit:shared.typing.configurations, unit:shared.typing.expression_soundness, unit:shared.typing.bindings, unit:shared.typing.steps, unit:shared.typing.erasure.",
